y're  clean you put them away and you think  i've accomplished something in my day i  get to experience that  three four hundred times a day every  single customer that walks in gets a  slice of pizza that feedback loop is so  tight that i don't know for me that  that's that's kind of all you need to  feel happy  for cbs saturday morning jamie wax  venice california  very nice very nice because already i'm  almost done we typically wait until  after the piece airs just i know i know  elaine and michelle and then i had to  join you too like you guys are  immediately digging in 15 seconds it was  great oh i didn't realize there was a  formal protocol involved jeff floor no  jeff's always  yummy  um look at this though it's right  spectacular did this look great marcy  thank you for all this thank you marcie  welcome marcy's here helping to the dish  master yes um coordinating all this wow  it looks really great and you know we've  heard this from so many chefs in the  past couple years is that they just want  to open a place and strip away all the  extra junk right and they just want to  make real food for real people right and  i love the fact that he has trained  literally at the highest levels eric  repair mary institute of america but  what does he want to do he chooses to  use that mastery of his craft to make it  more accessible to more people and and  meatballs by the way so comforting  especially at this hour in the morning  at 8 30 and brussels sprouts highly  recommend it everyone so good

